# ImmiGO Cursor Rules

The canonical contract is [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Read it first. This file is a thin adapter.

## Non-negotiables

- Supabase Auth/Postgres/RLS own auth and user data; Amplify Gen 2 owns backend hosting, API Gateway, Lambda, and storage.
- Handlers are raw API Gateway handlers. No Express, `serverless-http`, or new framework.
- Civics grading is server-side.
- Preserve API contracts, RLS, i18n/RTL, accessibility, and cleanup behavior.
- Tests exercise production code; never copy production logic into a test.
- Never delete, skip, or weaken a feature test to make CI pass.
- No secrets in `VITE_*`, client code, logs, tests, or commits.
- No new runtime dependency without approval.

## Workflow

Identify the feature ID in `docs/features.json`, read the mapped tests, add a failing test, make the smallest fix, run `npm run verify`, update the registry, and attach the change receipt from `AGENTS.md`.

Stop and ask for protected behavior, schema, auth, API contract, dependency, or broad refactor changes.
